hat the fish (not the row) is the independent unit is consistent with the data.\",\"The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: its per-fish table shows four trials per fish (repeated measurements per unit), while the Analysis section and the [selected-result] statement say all 20 rows were pooled 'as independent observations, one observation per row' into scipy.stats.binomtest with n = 20 and 'no grouping or weighting of rows'.\",\"The binomial test is row-independent, so entering the 20 pseudo-replicated trials as n independent Bernoulli observations treats repeated measurements from the same fish as independent; the significance claim (p = 0.0414 < 0.05) depends on n = 20 rather than the 5 independent fish, and the report's own table shows between-fish heterogeneity (e.g., AR-31 with 1/4 hits).\",\"No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock.\"]}","structured_output":{"declaration_consistent":true,"selected_report_demonstration":"issue","lock_follows_declaration":"not-applicable-no-lock","reasons":["Declared independent-unit column fish_tag is present in the frozen data/input.csv header and matches the translation receipt's extracted token and parsed header.","The frozen data contain exactly five distinct fish_tag values (AR-11, AR-14, AR-22, AR-27, AR-31), each with four rows, matching the data description's five fish with four sessions each, so the declaration that the fish (not the row) is the independent unit is consistent with the data.","The selected report demonstrates the issue on its face: its per-fish table shows four trials per fish (repeated measurements per unit), while the Analysis section and the [selected-result] statement say all 20 rows were pooled 'as independent observations, one observation per row' into scipy.stats.binomtest with n = 20 and 'no grouping or weighting of rows'.","The binomial test is row-independent, so entering the 20 pseudo-replicated trials as n independent Bernoulli observations treats repeated measurements from the same fish as independent; the significance claim (p = 0.0414 < 0.05) depends on n = 20 rather than the 5 independent fish, and the report's own table shows between-fish heterogeneity (e.g., AR-31 with 1/4 hits).","No authority lock was minted, so lock_follows_declaration is not-applicable-no-lock."]},"ttft_ms":6299,"ttft_stream_ms":1632,"time_to_request_ms":17,"type":"result","duration_ms":18149,"uuid":"c48231c4-9439-47d2-aa15-806ed940675e"}
